<odoo noupdate="1">
    <!-- WDGAP S2-C — the bank directory beyond Vietnam: the main Indonesian,
         Singaporean and Indian banks, with their public national codes, so a
         bank name recorded on an employee's account ("BCA", "Bank Central
         Asia") resolves to one bank and its code. noupdate: a company's
         corrections survive every upgrade.

         SOURCES (also in WDGAP_S2C_REPORT.md):
         * Singapore — OCBC "ACH Bank and Branch Code Guide" (as at 09 Dec
           2011), https://www.ocbc.com/assets/pdf/ach-bank-and-branch-code-guide.pdf :
           OCBC 7339, UOB 7375, DBS 7171, POSB 7171 (branch 081 for every
           POSB account), HSBC 7232, Standard Chartered 7144. A bank's own
           published document, but from 2011 — check before the first file.
         * Indonesia — INFERRED from public bank-code lists in the press
           (Bisnis.com 2022-01-27, CNN Indonesia 2021-07-22, Kompas TV), not
           Bank Indonesia's own list: BCA 014, Mandiri 008, BNI 009, BRI 002,
           BTN 200, CIMB Niaga 022, Permata 013, Danamon 011, BSI 451 (the
           press also gives 427 / 422 for the banks BSI merged).
         * India — INFERRED: the first four letters of every IFSC of the bank
           (the RBI IFSC scheme: 4 letters, a 0, 6 characters — confirmed by
           ICICI's published "File Format for Bulk upload in CIB"). The
           directory cannot give a branch's full IFSC; a bank file for India
           needs the IFSC recorded on the person's account.
         Vietnamese rows stay in vn_bank_registry_data.xml with no country. -->

